                        "entry_id": "64ccad17-f024-3b23-baab-8bae8b8297cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A ritual fire created by friction."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b949aeef-5d10-406a-8f97-d209869821f5",
                                "sense_id": "78777585-4af3-3b54-a856-d4219c4e9660",
                                "text": "In Silesia, also, need-fires were often employed for the purpose of curing a murrain or preventing its spread."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5111ec1-3b24-41c7-a8ae-214f60744dcf",
                                "sense_id": "78777585-4af3-3b54-a856-d4219c4e9660",
                                "text": "Fire - divided into need-fire (kindled by friction - discussed under 'Waluburg's Night') and 'struck fire' (sparked by flint and steel - discussion under Thonar)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56cc7872-5531-4765-8807-c180fc662e97",
                                "sense_id": "78777585-4af3-3b54-a856-d4219c4e9660",
                                "text": "I built up the kindling in various stages in the base of the stove as I prepared to make my need-fire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15509b8a-3879-496e-83c6-a5277d7abe58",
                                "sense_id": "78777585-4af3-3b54-a856-d4219c4e9660",
                                "text": "When great pestilence is upon the land, old folklore tells of using a bow drill to make the need-fire, which is then used to cure cattle of their illness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
